{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>When he makes inherit to his sons et that which, etc.</b> And it does not say ״on the day he makes inherit that which will be his to his sons,״ to bring the word ״makes inherit״ close to the statement ״to his sons,״ to allude to the reasoning of the Sages who said (Bava Batra 13a) that the father is able to bequeath to one son among his sons more than what pertains to him according to the equal division." "<b>He may not make the firstborn, etc.</b> And if he does make firstborn he transgresses a negative commandment, and with this is resolved that which the Tosafot raised as a difficulty (Bava Batra 13a) there in the passage beginning ״the Talmud teaches״ concerning the reasoning of the Rabbis."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:22.298131964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}